{"items":[{"cards":[{"blocks":[{"text":"Define a family of interchangeable algorithms behind one interface, and let the caller choose one at runtime.","type":"lead"},{"text":"A **context** holds a **strategy** and delegates one varying decision to it. The context never learns which concrete strategy it has, so a new algorithm means a new class or lambda, not an edit to the context.","type":"p"},{"items":["**Varies:** one algorithm or policy (pricing, sorting, retry, compression).","**Stays stable:** the code that uses it.","**Chosen by:** the client or configuration, usually once per use."],"type":"bullets"},{"text":"In Java 8+ a one-method strategy is a functional interface, so a lambda or method reference is a complete strategy.","tone":"info","type":"callout"}],"role":"definition","type":"text"},{"expectedOutput":"NONE -> 50.00\nSPRING10 -> 45.00\nWELCOME -> 42.50","file":"Strategy.java","regions":{"client":[47,48],"concrete":[11,25],"context":[27,36],"lambda":[40,40],"select":[41,44],"strategy":[6,9]},"role":"implementation","source":"import java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.math.RoundingMode;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\n@FunctionalInterface\ninterface DiscountPolicy {\n    BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal subtotal);\n}\n\nrecord PercentOff(int percent) implements DiscountPolicy {\n    PercentOff {\n        if (percent < 0 || percent > 100) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"percent\");\n    }\n    public BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal subtotal) {\n        BigDecimal factor = BigDecimal.valueOf(100 - percent, 2);\n        return subtotal.multiply(factor).setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN);\n    }\n}\n\nrecord FlatOff(BigDecimal amount) implements DiscountPolicy {\n    public BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal subtotal) {\n        return subtotal.subtract(amount).max(BigDecimal.ZERO);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Checkout {\n    private final DiscountPolicy policy;\n\n    Checkout(DiscountPolicy policy) { this.policy = policy; }\n\n    BigDecimal total(List<BigDecimal> prices) {\n        BigDecimal subtotal = prices.stream().reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);\n        return policy.apply(subtotal);\n    }\n}\n\nclass Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        DiscountPolicy none = subtotal -> subtotal;\n        Map<String, DiscountPolicy> byCode = Map.of(\n            \"NONE\", none,\n            \"SPRING10\", new PercentOff(10),\n            \"WELCOME\", new FlatOff(new BigDecimal(\"7.50\")));\n        var prices = List.of(new BigDecimal(\"19.99\"), new BigDecimal(\"30.01\"));\n        for (String code : List.of(\"NONE\", \"SPRING10\", \"WELCOME\")) {\n            var checkout = new Checkout(byCode.get(code));\n            System.out.println(code + \" -> \" + checkout.total(prices));\n        }\n    }\n}","type":"code","walkthrough":[{"note":"The strategy interface: one method. `@FunctionalInterface` lets lambdas implement it and makes the compiler enforce that.","region":"strategy"},{"note":"Concrete strategies as records: immutable, validated in the compact constructor, each knowing only its own rule.","region":"concrete"},{"note":"The context takes a strategy in its constructor and delegates the one varying step. No `switch`, no `instanceof`.","region":"context"},{"note":"A lambda is a full strategy. Trivial rules need no class at all.","region":"lambda"},{"note":"Selection lives at the edge, in a map from promo code to policy. A new promo touches this map, never `Checkout`.","region":"select"},{"note":"The client pairs context with strategy and calls the context. The same `Checkout` prints three different totals.","region":"client"}]},{"blocks":[{"text":"Shipping quotes in an online shop.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Each carrier prices parcels differently: weight tables, zones, surcharges. The customer picks a carrier at checkout, finance wants to A/B test a flat rate, and a new carrier arrives every quarter. Each rule becomes a `ShippingQuote` strategy with its own unit tests, and the checkout service stays unchanged.","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["interface ShippingQuote { Money quote(Parcel p, Address to); }","","ShippingQuote dhl  = new DhlTableRate(rates);","ShippingQuote flat = (p, to) -> Money.eur(\"4.90\");","ShippingQuote chosen = flags.on(\"flat-shipping\", user) ? flat : dhl;","Money price = checkout.quoteWith(chosen, cart, address);"],"type":"code"},{"text":"Payoff: a new carrier is a new class plus one registry line. The flat-rate experiment is one lambda behind a flag.","tone":"positive","type":"callout"}],"role":"example","type":"text"},{"diagrams":[{"edges":[{"from":"checkout","label":"policy","rel":"aggregation","to":"policy"},{"from":"pct","rel":"realizes","to":"policy"},{"from":"flat","rel":"realizes","to":"policy"}],"kind":"class","nodes":[{"col":0.5,"id":"checkout","kind":"class","members":["- policy: DiscountPolicy","+ total(prices): BigDecimal"],"name":"Checkout","role":"Context","row":0},{"col":0.5,"id":"policy","kind":"interface","members":["+ apply(subtotal): BigDecimal"],"name":"DiscountPolicy","role":"Strategy","row":1},{"col":0,"id":"pct","kind":"record","members":["+ apply(subtotal)"],"name":"PercentOff","role":"ConcreteStrategy","row":2},{"col":1,"id":"flat","kind":"record","members":["+ apply(subtotal)"],"name":"FlatOff","role":"ConcreteStrategy","row":2}],"notes":[{"attachTo":"policy","text":"a lambda also implements it"}],"title":"Class"},{"fragments":[],"kind":"sequence","messages":[{"from":"client","label":"new Checkout(policy)","style":"create","to":"checkout"},{"from":"client","label":"total(prices)","style":"call","to":"checkout"},{"from":"checkout","label":"apply(subtotal)","style":"call","to":"policy"},{"from":"policy","label":"discounted","style":"return","to":"checkout"},{"from":"checkout","label":"total","style":"return","to":"client"}],"participants":[{"id":"client","name":"Client"},{"id":"checkout","name":"Checkout","role":"Context"},{"id":"policy","name":"PercentOff","role":"Strategy"}],"title":"Sequence"}],"role":"structure","type":"diagram"},{"lists":[{"items":["Several variants of one algorithm must be swappable at runtime.","A growing `switch` on a type or code picks behaviour.","You want each rule unit-tested in isolation."],"title":"Use when","tone":"positive"},{"items":["There are two variants that will never change: an `if` is clearer.","Variants need different inputs, so one interface cannot fit them all."],"title":"Avoid when","tone":"negative"},{"items":["Context checking `instanceof` on its strategy, which defeats the pattern.","Clients must now know every strategy; hide the choice behind a registry or factory.","Stateful strategies shared across threads."],"title":"Pitfalls","tone":"warning"},{"items":["An interface plus classes for a rule that a lambda would cover.","A `StrategyFactoryProvider` with a single implementation."],"title":"Overuse smells","tone":"warning"},{"items":["Functional interfaces and lambdas replace most strategy class hierarchies.","For a closed set of data-driven rules, a sealed interface plus `switch` pattern matching can be simpler."],"title":"Modern Java","tone":"info"}],"role":"tradeoffs","type":"lists"},{"role":"compare","rows":[{"difference":"Same shape, different intent. With State the object switches its own state as events arrive and the states know each other. With Strategy the client chooses and strategies are independent.","ref":"state","relation":"lookAlike"},{"difference":"Template Method varies steps through inheritance, fixed at compile time. Strategy varies the whole algorithm through composition, at runtime.","ref":"template-method","relation":"alternative"},{"difference":"A command packages a request to run, queue or undo later. A strategy answers *how* to do one job right now.","ref":"command","relation":"oftenConfused"},{"difference":"Decorator changes an object's behaviour by wrapping it from the outside; Strategy replaces its internals.","ref":"decorator","relation":"alternative"},{"difference":"A factory or registry often picks the strategy from configuration, and DI injects it.","ref":"factory-method","relation":"combines"}],"type":"comparison"},{"entries":[{"detail":"Passed to `List.sort`, `TreeMap` and `Collections.max` to choose the ordering algorithm.","name":"java.util.Comparator","where":"JDK"},{"detail":"`ThreadPoolExecutor` delegates overflow to a policy: `AbortPolicy`, `CallerRunsPolicy`, `DiscardPolicy`.","name":"RejectedExecutionHandler","where":"JDK"},{"detail":"`BCryptPasswordEncoder` and `Argon2PasswordEncoder` are interchangeable; `DelegatingPasswordEncoder` picks one per stored hash.","name":"PasswordEncoder","where":"Spring Security"},{"detail":"`SNAKE_CASE` and `KEBAB_CASE` change how property names map to JSON.","name":"PropertyNamingStrategies","where":"Jackson"},{"detail":"`RollingUpdate` or `Recreate`: the same controller with a different rollout algorithm.","name":"Deployment spec.strategy","where":"Kubernetes"}],"role":"sightings","type":"references"}],"exercises":[{"compile":{"template":["import java.io.IOException;","import java.nio.file.*;","interface Codec { String extension(); byte[] encode(byte[] raw); }","{{code}}"]},"id":"spot-1","kind":"identify","lines":["final class BackupJob {","    private final Codec codec;","    BackupJob(Codec codec) { this.codec = codec; }","","    void run(Path file) throws IOException {","        byte[] raw = Files.readAllBytes(file);","        Path out = file.resolveSibling(file.getFileName() + codec.extension());","        Files.write(out, codec.encode(raw));","    }","}","// GzipCodec, ZstdCodec, NoopCodec; chosen from the --codec flag"],"options":[{"correct":true,"ref":"strategy","why":"The job delegates one varying algorithm (encoding) to an injected, interchangeable `Codec`."},{"ref":"state","why":"Nothing transitions: the codec is fixed for the job's life and never replaces itself."},{"ref":"bridge","why":"There is no second abstraction hierarchy being developed independently; it is one job with one pluggable step."},{"ref":"template-method","why":"There is no abstract superclass with overridable steps; the variation comes through composition."}],"prompt":"Which pattern is this?"},{"id":"pick-1","kind":"choose","options":[{"correct":true,"ref":"strategy","why":"One varying algorithm, selected from outside per request, with new variants added without touching the engine."},{"ref":"state","why":"There is no lifecycle and no transitions; the rule does not change itself as events arrive."},{"ref":"template-method","why":"A subclass per country fixes the choice at compile time and couples every rule to one base-class skeleton."},{"ref":"chain-of-responsibility","why":"The responsible rule is known up front from the address; there is nothing to pass along a chain."}],"prompt":"Which pattern fits best?","scenario":"A tax engine computes VAT differently per country. The rule is chosen at checkout from the shipping address, new countries are added monthly, and a rule never changes during one calculation."},{"compile":{"template":["import java.math.BigDecimal;","interface DiscountPolicy { BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal s); }","record PercentOff(int percent) implements DiscountPolicy { public BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal s) { return s; } }","{{code}}"]},"explanation":"The context inspects a concrete strategy, so every new policy can force an edit here. Put the cap in a decorating policy, e.g. `capped(policy, 50)`, or in the strategy itself.","flawLines":[7],"id":"flaw-1","kind":"tapLine","lines":["final class Checkout {","    private final DiscountPolicy policy;","","    Checkout(DiscountPolicy policy) { this.policy = policy; }","","    BigDecimal total(BigDecimal subtotal) {","        if (policy instanceof PercentOff p && p.percent() > 50) {","            return subtotal; // block deep discounts","        }","        return policy.apply(subtotal);","    }","}"],"prompt":"Tap the line that breaks the Strategy pattern."},{"blocks":[["String code = request.promoCode();"],["DiscountPolicy policy = policies.getOrDefault(code, s -> s);"],["Checkout checkout = new Checkout(policy);"],["BigDecimal total = checkout.total(cart.prices());"],["receipt.print(total);"]],"compile":{"template":["import java.math.BigDecimal;","import java.util.*;","interface DiscountPolicy { BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal s); }","final class Checkout { private final DiscountPolicy p; Checkout(DiscountPolicy p) { this.p = p; }","  BigDecimal total(List<BigDecimal> xs) { return p.apply(xs.stream().reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add)); } }","record Request(String promoCode) {}","record Cart(List<BigDecimal> prices) {}","interface Receipt { void print(BigDecimal total); }","class Snippet { void run(Request request, Map<String, DiscountPolicy> policies, Cart cart, Receipt receipt) {","{{code}}","} }"]},"explanation":"Read the input, resolve the strategy at the edge, inject it into the context, then delegate. The context never sees the promo code.","id":"order-1","kind":"reorder","prompt":"Order the request flow so that each line only uses what came before."},{"id":"recall-1","keyPoints":["One varying algorithm behind one interface","Context delegates and never inspects the concrete type","The client or config chooses, often by injection","State changes itself and knows the transitions; Strategy is chosen from outside","In modern Java a lambda can be the strategy"],"kind":"recall","modelAnswer":[{"text":"Strategy pulls one varying algorithm out of a class behind an interface. The context delegates to whatever strategy it was given, and the client or configuration chooses it, usually at construction. Unlike State, strategies don't know each other and the context doesn't swap them in response to its own events.","type":"p"}],"prompt":"Explain Strategy in your own words: what varies, who chooses, and how it differs from State."}],"id":"strategy"}],"topic":{"categories":[{"id":"foundations","summary":"Principles every pattern builds on.","template":"principle","title":"Foundations"},{"id":"creational","summary":"How objects get made.","template":"pattern","title":"Creational"},{"id":"structural","summary":"How objects are composed into larger structures.","template":"pattern","title":"Structural"},{"id":"behavioral","summary":"How objects share responsibility and communicate.","template":"pattern","title":"Behavioral"},{"id":"concurrency","summary":"Coordinating work across threads.","template":"pattern","title":"Concurrency"},{"id":"enterprise","summary":"Structuring applications and their data access.","template":"pattern","title":"Enterprise & Architecture"},{"id":"resilience","summary":"Keeping distributed systems working when parts fail.","template":"pattern","title":"Resilience & Cloud"}],"codeLanguage":"java","id":"design-patterns","items":[{"aliases":["SRP","Single Responsibility Principle"],"category":"foundations","difficulty":1,"id":"srp","intent":"Give each class one reason to change.","title":"Single Responsibility"},{"aliases":["OCP","Open/Closed Principle"],"category":"foundations","difficulty":1,"id":"ocp","intent":"Extend behavior by adding code, not by editing working code.","title":"Open/Closed"},{"aliases":["LSP","Liskov Substitution Principle"],"category":"foundations","difficulty":2,"id":"lsp","intent":"A subtype must be usable anywhere its supertype is, without surprises.","title":"Liskov Substitution"},{"aliases":["ISP","Interface Segregation Principle"],"category":"foundations","difficulty":2,"id":"isp","intent":"Prefer several small, focused interfaces to one fat one.","title":"Interface Segregation"},{"aliases":["DIP","Dependency Inversion Principle"],"category":"foundations","difficulty":2,"id":"dip","intent":"Depend on abstractions; let low-level details implement what high-level code needs.","title":"Dependency Inversion"},{"aliases":["Favor Composition","Has-a over Is-a"],"category":"foundations","difficulty":2,"id":"composition-over-inheritance","intent":"Reuse behavior by holding collaborators, not by extending classes.","title":"Composition over Inheritance"},{"aliases":["Code to an Interface","Program to a Supertype"],"category":"foundations","difficulty":2,"id":"program-to-interface","intent":"Depend on what a type can do, not on the concrete class that does it.","title":"Program to an Interface"},{"aliases":["Law of Demeter","Principle of Least Knowledge"],"category":"foundations","difficulty":2,"id":"tell-dont-ask","intent":"Tell objects what to do instead of pulling out their state to decide for them.","title":"Tell, Don't Ask"},{"aliases":["Virtual Constructor"],"category":"creational","difficulty":1,"id":"factory-method","intent":"Let a method, overridable or injectable, decide which concrete class to create.","title":"Factory Method"},{"aliases":["Kit"],"category":"creational","difficulty":3,"id":"abstract-factory","intent":"Create whole families of related objects without naming their concrete classes.","title":"Abstract Factory"},{"aliases":["Fluent Builder"],"category":"creational","difficulty":1,"id":"builder","intent":"Assemble a complex object step by step and validate it when built.","title":"Builder"},{"aliases":["Clone"],"category":"creational","difficulty":2,"id":"prototype","intent":"Create new objects by copying an existing one.","title":"Prototype"},{"aliases":["Single Instance"],"category":"creational","difficulty":2,"id":"singleton","intent":"Guarantee one instance per scope; today usually an enum or a DI-managed singleton.","title":"Singleton"},{"aliases":["Wrapper"],"category":"structural","difficulty":1,"id":"adapter","intent":"Make an incompatible interface look like the one your code expects.","title":"Adapter"},{"aliases":["Handle/Body"],"category":"structural","difficulty":2,"id":"bridge","intent":"Split an abstraction from its implementation so each can vary on its own.","title":"Bridge"},{"aliases":["Object Tree"],"category":"structural","difficulty":2,"id":"composite","intent":"Treat single objects and groups of objects through one interface.","title":"Composite"},{"aliases":["Wrapper"],"category":"structural","difficulty":2,"id":"decorator","intent":"Add behavior to an object by wrapping it in another object with the same interface.","title":"Decorator"},{"aliases":["Simplified Interface"],"category":"structural","difficulty":2,"id":"facade","intent":"Offer one simple entry point to a complex subsystem.","title":"Facade"},{"aliases":["Cache"],"category":"structural","difficulty":3,"id":"flyweight","intent":"Share immutable state between many objects to save memory.","title":"Flyweight"},{"aliases":["Surrogate"],"category":"structural","difficulty":2,"id":"proxy","intent":"Stand in for another object to control access, defer work, or add checks.","title":"Proxy"},{"aliases":["Chain of Command","Handler Chain"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":2,"id":"chain-of-responsibility","intent":"Pass a request along a chain of handlers until one deals with it.","title":"Chain of Responsibility"},{"aliases":["Action","Transaction"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":2,"id":"command","intent":"Wrap a request in an object so it can be queued, logged, retried or undone.","title":"Command"},{"aliases":[],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":3,"id":"interpreter","intent":"Represent a small language as a grammar of classes and evaluate sentences in it.","title":"Interpreter"},{"aliases":["Cursor"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":1,"id":"iterator","intent":"Walk a collection without exposing how it is stored.","title":"Iterator"},{"aliases":["Controller"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":2,"id":"mediator","intent":"Centralize how a group of objects talk to each other.","title":"Mediator"},{"aliases":["Snapshot","Token"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":2,"id":"memento","intent":"Capture an object's state so it can be restored later without breaking encapsulation.","title":"Memento"},{"aliases":["Publish-Subscribe","Listener","Dependents"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":2,"id":"observer","intent":"Notify any number of dependents when an object changes.","title":"Observer"},{"aliases":["Objects for States"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":2,"id":"state","intent":"Let an object change its behavior when its internal state changes.","title":"State"},{"aliases":["Policy"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":1,"id":"strategy","intent":"Swap one algorithm for another behind a single interface.","title":"Strategy"},{"aliases":[],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":2,"id":"template-method","intent":"Fix the skeleton of an algorithm in a base class and let subclasses fill in the steps.","title":"Template Method"},{"aliases":["Double Dispatch"],"category":"behavioral","difficulty":3,"id":"visitor","intent":"Add new operations to a class hierarchy without changing the classes.","title":"Visitor"},{"aliases":["Value Object"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":1,"id":"immutable-object","intent":"Share state safely between threads by never changing it.","title":"Immutable Object"},{"aliases":["Monitor Object","Guarded Wait"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":2,"id":"guarded-suspension","intent":"Make a thread wait until a condition holds before it proceeds.","title":"Guarded Suspension"},{"aliases":["Bounded Buffer"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":2,"id":"producer-consumer","intent":"Decouple threads that make work from threads that do it with a queue.","title":"Producer-Consumer"},{"aliases":["Worker Pool","Executor"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":1,"id":"thread-pool","intent":"Reuse a fixed set of worker threads for many short tasks.","title":"Thread Pool"},{"aliases":["CompletableFuture","Promise"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":2,"id":"future-promise","intent":"Represent a result that is not ready yet and compose what happens when it is.","title":"Future / Promise"},{"aliases":["Shared-Exclusive Lock"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":2,"id":"read-write-lock","intent":"Allow many concurrent readers but only one writer.","title":"Read-Write Lock"},{"aliases":["DCL"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":3,"id":"double-checked-locking","intent":"Avoid locking on every access to a lazily created object; mostly obsolete today.","title":"Double-Checked Locking"},{"aliases":["Actor"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":3,"id":"active-object","intent":"Give an object its own thread and queue so callers invoke it asynchronously.","title":"Active Object"},{"aliases":["Event Loop","Dispatcher"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":3,"id":"reactor","intent":"Handle many I/O sources on few threads by dispatching ready events to handlers.","title":"Reactor"},{"aliases":["Divide and Conquer"],"category":"concurrency","difficulty":3,"id":"fork-join","intent":"Split a task into subtasks, run them in parallel, and combine the results.","title":"Fork-Join"},{"aliases":["N-Tier","Layers"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":1,"id":"layered-architecture","intent":"Organize code into layers where each only talks to the layer below.","title":"Layered Architecture"},{"aliases":["Ports and Adapters","Clean Architecture"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":2,"id":"hexagonal","intent":"Keep the domain in the center and plug the outside world in through ports and adapters.","title":"Hexagonal Architecture"},{"aliases":["MVC"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":2,"id":"mvc","intent":"Separate data, presentation and input handling into three roles.","title":"Model-View-Controller"},{"aliases":["MVVM"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":2,"id":"mvvm","intent":"Bind a view to a view model that exposes state and commands, free of UI classes.","title":"Model-View-ViewModel"},{"aliases":["DI","Inversion of Control"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":1,"id":"dependency-injection","intent":"Hand an object its collaborators instead of letting it create or look them up.","title":"Dependency Injection"},{"aliases":["Registry"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":2,"id":"service-locator","intent":"Look up services from a global registry; the pattern DI exists to replace.","title":"Service Locator"},{"aliases":["Collection-like Persistence"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":2,"id":"repository","intent":"Hide storage behind a collection-like interface for domain objects.","title":"Repository"},{"aliases":[],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":3,"id":"unit-of-work","intent":"Track changes during a business transaction and commit them together.","title":"Unit of Work"},{"aliases":["ORM Mapper"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":3,"id":"data-mapper","intent":"Move data between objects and a database while keeping them ignorant of each other.","title":"Data Mapper"},{"aliases":[],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":3,"id":"active-record","intent":"An object wraps a database row and knows how to save and load itself.","title":"Active Record"},{"aliases":["Predicate Object"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":3,"id":"specification","intent":"Express a business rule as a small object that can be combined and reused.","title":"Specification"},{"aliases":["DTO","Transfer Object"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":2,"id":"dto","intent":"Carry data across a boundary in a plain object shaped for that boundary.","title":"Data Transfer Object"},{"aliases":[],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":3,"id":"domain-event","intent":"Record that something meaningful happened in the domain so other parts can react.","title":"Domain Event"},{"aliases":["Command Query Responsibility Segregation"],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":3,"id":"cqrs","intent":"Use separate models for changing state and for reading it.","title":"CQRS"},{"aliases":[],"category":"enterprise","difficulty":3,"id":"event-sourcing","intent":"Store the sequence of events that happened and derive current state from them.","title":"Event Sourcing"},{"aliases":["Deadline"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":1,"id":"timeout","intent":"Bound how long you wait for a call so a slow dependency cannot hold you hostage.","title":"Timeout"},{"aliases":["Exponential Backoff","Retry","Jitter"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":1,"id":"retry-backoff","intent":"Retry transient failures with growing, randomized delays.","title":"Retry with Backoff"},{"aliases":["Fallback"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":2,"id":"circuit-breaker","intent":"Stop calling a failing dependency for a while and fail fast or fall back.","title":"Circuit Breaker"},{"aliases":["Isolation"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":2,"id":"bulkhead","intent":"Isolate resources per consumer so one failure cannot sink everything.","title":"Bulkhead"},{"aliases":["Throttling","Token Bucket"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":2,"id":"rate-limiter","intent":"Cap how many requests are accepted per unit of time.","title":"Rate Limiter"},{"aliases":["Idempotent Receiver","Deduplication"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":3,"id":"idempotent-consumer","intent":"Make processing a message twice have the same effect as once.","title":"Idempotent Consumer"},{"aliases":["Outbox"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":3,"id":"transactional-outbox","intent":"Write the message in the same transaction as the data, then publish it reliably.","title":"Transactional Outbox"},{"aliases":["Process Manager","Long-Running Transaction"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":3,"id":"saga","intent":"Coordinate a multi-service workflow with local transactions and compensations.","title":"Saga"},{"aliases":["Lazy Loading Cache"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":2,"id":"cache-aside","intent":"Load data into a cache on demand and keep the database as the source of truth.","title":"Cache-Aside"},{"aliases":["Work Queue"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":3,"id":"competing-consumers","intent":"Let several consumers pull from one queue to scale throughput.","title":"Competing Consumers"},{"aliases":["Edge Service"],"category":"resilience","difficulty":2,"id":"api-gateway","intent":"Offer clients one entry point that routes, aggregates and secures calls to services.","title":"API Gateway"},{"aliases":[],"category":"resilience","difficulty":2,"id":"sidecar","intent":"Run a helper process next to a service to provide cross-cutting capabilities.","title":"Sidecar"},{"aliases":[],"category":"resilience","difficulty":2,"id":"ambassador","intent":"Put a helper next to a client to handle its outbound calls.","title":"Ambassador"},{"aliases":[],"category":"resilience","difficulty":2,"id":"strangler-fig","intent":"Replace a legacy system piece by piece behind a routing facade.","title":"Strangler Fig"}],"javaRelease":21,"path":[{"items":["srp","ocp","lsp","isp","dip","composition-over-inheritance","program-to-interface","tell-dont-ask"],"title":"Foundations"},{"items":["strategy","factory-method","builder","adapter","decorator","observer","template-method","facade"],"title":"First patterns"},{"items":["iterator","command","state","composite","proxy","singleton","chain-of-responsibility","abstract-factory"],"title":"Core GoF"},{"items":["bridge","mediator","memento","prototype","flyweight","visitor","interpreter"],"title":"Advanced GoF"},{"items":["layered-architecture","dependency-injection","service-locator","dto","mvc","mvvm","hexagonal","repository","data-mapper","active-record","unit-of-work","specification","domain-event"],"title":"Application architecture"},{"items":["immutable-object","thread-pool","future-promise","producer-consumer","guarded-suspension","read-write-lock","double-checked-locking","fork-join","active-object","reactor"],"title":"Concurrency"},{"items":["timeout","retry-backoff","circuit-breaker","bulkhead","rate-limiter","cache-aside","idempotent-consumer","competing-consumers"],"title":"Resilience"},{"items":["api-gateway","sidecar","ambassador","strangler-fig","transactional-outbox","saga","cqrs","event-sourcing"],"title":"Distributed systems"}],"requiredExercises":[["identify"],["choose"],["tapLine","reorder"],["recall"]],"roles":{"compare":{"symbol":"arrow.left.arrow.right","title":"Compare & relate","type":"comparison"},"definition":{"symbol":"text.book.closed","title":"Definition","type":"text"},"example":{"symbol":"building.2","title":"Example of use","type":"text"},"implementation":{"symbol":"chevron.left.forwardslash.chevron.right","title":"Implementation","type":"code"},"sightings":{"symbol":"binoculars","title":"In the wild","type":"references"},"structure":{"symbol":"point.3.connected.trianglepath.dotted","title":"Structure","type":"diagram"},"tradeoffs":{"symbol":"scale.3d","title":"When to use","type":"lists"}},"schemaVersion":1,"sortOrder":0,"subtitle":"GoF, concurrency, enterprise and resilience patterns in modern Java","symbol":"square.stack.3d.up","templates":{"pattern":{"roles":["definition","implementation","example","structure","tradeoffs","compare","sightings"]},"principle":{"optionalRoles":["structure"],"roles":["definition","implementation","example","tradeoffs","compare","sightings"]}},"title":"Design Patterns"}}
